    "body": "13 context-menu/palette refactorings built on the round-trip (#2374): parse buffer -> transform term -> print -> splice. Ids survive, so probes, statics, and incremental caches do too.\r\n\r\n### Gestural - Naming\r\n- **Inline Let**: `let x = 1 + 2 in x + 3` -> `1 + 2 + 3`; offered at the let, its binder, or any occurrence of `x`. Parens only where a reparse oracle proves the bare form changes the program: `let x = 1 + 2 in 3 + x` -> `3 + (1 + 2)`.\r\n- **Add Parameter**: `let f = fun x -> x + 1 in f(2)` -> `let f = fun (x, x1) -> x + 1 in f(2, ?)` \u2014 definition and every call site atomically, including recursive calls. Handles `let f(x) = x + 1 in f(2)` -> `let f(x, x1) = x + 1 in f(2, ?)` and annotated bindings (`Int -> Int` becomes `(Int, ?) -> Int`). Gated off when `f` is used as a bare value (`map(f, xs)`).\r\n- **Hoist Let**: `fun n -> let x = 2 in x + n` -> `let x = 2 in fun n -> x + n` \u2014 one level per invocation (through chains, out of defs, out of lambdas). The explicit opt-in to evaluation-count changes that Extract avoids.\r\n- **Sink Let**: `let x = 2 in case m | 1 => x | _ => 0 end` -> `case m | 1 => let x = 2 in x | _ => 0 end` \u2014 into the single arm/branch/lambda that uses the binding. Both movements are scope-gated and shadow-aware; blocked moves are simply not offered.\r\n- **Extract to Let**: binds at the nearest enclosing line \u2014 `let a = 1 in g(f(2))` extracting `f(2)` -> `let a = 1 in let x = f(2) in g(x)`; a def-site hoists above its line (`let a = g(f(2)) in ...` -> `let x = f(2) in let a = g(x) in ...`). Never escapes a lambda or case arm, so evaluation count/conditionality never changes.\r\n\r\n### Gestural - Choice\r\n- **Add Missing Case Arm**: `case b | true => 1 end` -> `case b | true => 1 | false => ? end`, one arm per invocation from the Coverage witness \u2014 real constructors for finite domains (`Green`), literals wildified for infinite ones (`case n | 1 => 2 end` gains `| _ => ?`). Label names the witness: \"Add Arm | false\".\r\n\r\n### Naming (non-gestural)\r\n- **Rename (bind free occurrences)**: rename a binder by ordinary editing \u2014 `let vel = 1 in v + v` (was `v`) marks the old uses free, and the binder token offers \"Rename v to vel\" -> `let vel = 1 in vel + vel`. Stateless: reconstructed from scope state, no edit tracking. Works at let heads, `f(x)`-sugar names and params, fun params, and case-arm pats; per-occurrence shadow-precise.\r\n- **Remove Unused Let**: `let x = 1 in 2 + 2` -> `2 + 2`; gated on the statics unused-binding warning. Works on annotated heads and unused `f(x)`-sugar fns.\r\n\r\n### Equational (syntactic)\r\n- **Convert to Case**: `if a then 1 else 2` -> `case a | true => 1 | false => 2 end`.\r\n- **Convert to If**: the inverse, either arm order: `case a | false => 2 | true => 1 end` -> `if a then 1 else 2`.\r\n- **Negate & Swap Branches**: `if a && b then 1 else 2` -> `if !(a && b) then 2 else 1` \u2014 arms swap with their formatting untouched; condition parens by the oracle (`if a ...` gives bare `!a`).\r\n- **Eta-Reduce**: `fun y -> f(y)` -> `f`, gated on `y` not occurring in `f`.\r\n\r\n### Equational (semantic)\r\n- **Add Type Annotation**: `let x = 1 + 2 in x` -> `let x : Int = 1 + 2 in x`, type from statics; only offered when the inferred type is hole-free. Oracle-parenthesized: `let p = (1, true) in p` -> `let p : (Int,Bool) = (1, true) in p`.\r\n\r\n\r\nFormatting is preserved by construction: whitespace runs belong to line slots and transforms move/copy them explicitly, so multiline layouts survive swaps, extractions, and conversions. Menu gating never prints, parses, or runs the oracle (invocation only). ~110 tests in Test_Refactor.re.\r\n\r\nStacked on #2374; retarget to dev when it merges.\r\n\r\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
